<title>UK: Novorossiisk oil port reopens as weather improves.</title>
<headline>Novorossiisk oil port reopens as weather improves.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's leading oil export terminal at Novorossiisk on the Black Sea reopened on Friday after bad weather disrupted operations for much of Thursday, a shipping source said.</p>
<p>A combination of high winds, swell and thunderstorms kept the port closed from 1045 to 2145 local time on Thursday, the source said.</p>
<p>Operations resumed early Friday with a small crude tanker starting to load at berth number two. A second crude tanker and a fuel oil vessel were alongside other berths.</p>
<p>Other Black Sea and Baltic ports were working normally on Friday, the source said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
